				<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>There is a short movie &#8211; called <strong>If We Took a Holiday</strong> &#8211; that<strong> Madonna</strong>&#8216;s fans could love and is being premiered this days at aGLIFF and at The Chicago LGBT International Film Festival.</p>
<p><strong>If We Took a Holiday</strong> is a comedic short film which features a <strong>Madonna impersonator</strong> who decides to impersonate <strong>Madonna</strong> all day long as a birthday gift for her gay best friend, who recently broke up with his boyfriend.</p>
<p><strong>If We Took a Holiday</strong> is directed by Glenn Gaylord and written by Gaylord, Nadya Ginsburg and Dennis Hensley.</p>
